     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice that limit. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease confirm what you intended. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** That's 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals.** That's 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg per dose.** These are common doses, and 1700 may have been a typo.\n- **Another dose.** If 1700 mg is the dose you meant, tell me and I'll add a note to the order.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
